      "content": "If the cost of maintenance is just draining you further, then exiting the game isn't a failure; it's a strategic withdrawal. You've already proven you can build something massive, and now you have the clarity to recognize when the cost outweighs the return. Think of it less as a final loss and more as finally closing a chapter that was never going to pay off. There is a quiet dignity in choosing when to stop the drain.",
